Content inside `{{ }}` should be highlighted as `.js`. Attributes starting with `v-*`, `:`, `@` and `#` should be highlighted as `.js` but I could not make it work. Also comments are not working inside sub-syntax (bug?).

Example vue component with SFC syntax variantions for script and style blocks:

```vue
<template>
  <div 
    v-for="index in 5" 
    :key="index"
    class="wrapper"
    @click="onClick">
    <div
      :class="{ [$style.red]: index == 1 }"
      class="item">
      {{ text }} {{ index }} Text
    </div>
  </div>
  <SomeOtherComponent>
    <template #default="{ text }">
      <span>{{ text }}</span>
    </template>
  </SomeOtherComponent>
</template>

<script setup>
const theme = {
  color: 'red'
}
</script>

<script>
export default {
  name: 'SampleComponent',
  data() {
    return {
      text: 'Sample'
    }
  },
  methods: {
    onClick() {
      alert('Click!')
    }
  }
}
</script>

<style module>
.red {
  color: v-bind('theme.color');
}
</style>

<style scoped lang="scss">
.wrapper {
  border: 1px solid;
  padding: 1rem;

  .item {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;

    &:last-child {
      margin-bottom: 0;
    }
  }
}
</style>
```

